     2	
     3	## Wet lab
     4	- Cells: adherent reporter line (identity blinded), 96-well imaging plate with optical bottom, all 96 wells in use.
     5	- Compounds: eight blinded test compounds, 8-point 3-fold series from 30 uM, one well per concentration; vehicle = DMSO (0.3% in every well); REF-INH = reference inhibitor of the marker pathway at 10 uM. Dispensed acoustically according to plate_layout.tsv, 48 h treatment.
     6	- Incubation: 37 C / 5% CO2, standard polystyrene lid.
     7	- Fixation 4% PFA, permeabilisation 0.1% Triton X-100.
     8	- Staining: Alexa Fluor 488 conjugate against the marker protein, two PBS washes, wells left in 100 uL PBS.
     9	- Nuclear counterstain: Hoechst 33342 in the last wash.
    10	
    11	## Imaging
    12	- Automated widefield microscope, 10x / NA 0.45 air objective, sCMOS camera with 2 x 2 binning (1.3 um per pixel), 16 bit.
    13	- Channel 1: Hoechst (ex 385 nm). Channel 2: Alexa Fluor 488 (ex 475 nm). One field per well at the well centre, cropped to 320 x 320 pixels for transfer. Same exposure time for all wells of a channel.
    14	- Focus: hardware autofocus on the plate bottom.
    15	- Reference frames (flatfield/): average of 50 exposures of a uniform dye slide per channel and of 50 exposures with the shutter closed, recorded the same day.
    16	- Files are raw camera frames: no illumination, background or any other correction was applied.
    17	
    18	## Manual counts
    19	- 8 fields of this plate were counted by hand by two technicians with the point tool of the image viewer, following SOP IA-07 section 1 (annotations/). Fields were picked to cover untreated wells of the inner and outer plate area and wells of the highest and of intermediate concentrations.
